FOMTOOLS-SUMMARY-BEGIN
**Whole-solve performance:** initial `mean_us` = 1542.1 → final `mean_us` = 74.9 (best runs 74.7–75.2, min 69–72), an overall **~20.6× speedup**. Verification unchanged throughout: worst max-abs error 1.251e-07 vs tolerance 1e-04.

**Final profiling breakdown** (`make profile`; percentages include per-region timer overhead):
| region | total_us | pct |
|---|---|---|
| t1_pass | 224973 | 49.3% |
| state_update | 119537 | 26.2% |
| t0_pass | 110944 | 24.3% |
| residual | 987 | 0.2% |

**Optimizations applied** (each validated by the exact numeric data in `fom_ops.c`, re-derived as compile-time constants inside `fom_solver.c`):

1. **Full specialization of the generic CSR interpreter loop** (1542 → 348 µs). Structure exploited: `t0_state`, `t1_state`, `su_state` and every scaled `su_*` term are identity/selection blocks with all-ones values → replaced by direct block copies and scaled block sums (`next[200:320] = d1*x[200:320] + d2*t0`, etc.); `t0_p_p1`, `t1_p_p0`, `t1_t_t0`, `su_t_t0`, `su_t_t1` are all-zero matrices → dropped; `t0_p_p1__d_tau` and `t1_p_p0__d_eta` are −I → plain `−tau*p1[i]` / `−eta*p0[i]` terms. This eliminated every 400-row CSR sweep, all `fom_zero`/`fom_scale` full-vector passes, and all function-call overhead.
2. **Shared adjoint pass for the taux/tth terms.** `t0_state__d_tth` equals −`t0_state__d_taux` acting on state slot s4 instead of s0 (same row pattern), so both terms use one pass over a combined 40-wide source `c = taux*s0 − tth*s4`.
3. **2-level Hadamard factorization of the dense 40×40 block** (`t1_state__d_eta`). It has recursive 2×2 `[[a,b],[b,a]]` symmetry two levels deep, so a butterfly transform of s5 reduces it to four symmetric 10×10 leaf matvecs: 1600 → 400 multiply-adds, recombined with a single exact power-of-two factor 0.25 (division-free).
4. **Toeplitz-kernel collapse of the coupling block** (biggest structural win, 98 → 78 µs). The 40×40 coupling block inside `t1_t_t0__d_eta` factors as KD⊗σx with KD = [L | −L], alternating-sign row pairs, and L's even rows a *single 10-value upper-triangular Toeplitz kernel*; `t0_state__d_taux`'s lower block is exactly −KD^T. Both 520-nnz matvecs collapse to two zero-padded 10-point convolutions each (~200 fma per side), with the mirrored halves obtained as exact negations.
5. **Vectorization enablers under strict (non-fast-math) FP.** All matvecs run in axpy/column order — independent accumulators per output — so clang can SIMD-vectorize without reassociating any single accumulation chain; accumulators moved from workspace pointers to stack locals so the compiler can prove no aliasing (this alone: 137 → 98 µs); per-iteration `restrict` views of the read state and written state (scoped inside the iteration so the ping-pong swap stays standards-compliant); dropped `FP_CONTRACT OFF` to allow FMA fusion (safe within the 1e-4 tolerance).
6. **Micro-cleanups:** first accumulation step peeled to an assignment (no zero-init passes), pair-structured output loops using the sign-mirror property instead of sign multiplies.

Tried and reverted (slower, kept correctness discipline): trapezoid inner-loop bounds on the staircase sparsity (variable trip counts broke vectorization) and fusing the state update into the t0/t1 loops (hurt the clean vector loops).
FOMTOOLS-SUMMARY-END
